        }
      },
      "source_ids": [
        "S1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b3",
      "function": "explanation",
      "scene_type": "gb_principle",
      "spoken": "The solution: caissons. Huge wooden boxes were sunk to the bottom with compressed air. Inside, men dug in the dry until the box sat deep enough.",
      "data": {
        "headline": "The solution",
        "note": "caisson schematic",
        "pins": [
          {
            "anchor": "cny",
            "text": "Caisson",
            "at": "@caissons",
            "side": "up"
          }
        ],
        "rule": {
          "text": "Compressed air keeps the water out.",
          "at": "@compressed",
          "dy": 660
        }
      },
      "source_ids": [
        "S2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b4",
      "function": "demonstration",
      "scene_type": "gb_build",
      "spoken": "The caissons measured 102 by 172 feet. On the New York side they sank about 24 metres, on the Brooklyn side about 14. The bridge hangs from four main cables, each made of 5,434 wires.",
      "data": {
        "headline": "How it was built",
        "rows": [
          {
            "pos": "1",
            "part": "Caisson, feet",
            "qty": "102×172",
