    {
      "id": "b5",
      "function": "insight",
      "scene_type": "gb_proof",
      "spoken": "The price was high. About 110 men fell ill with decompression sickness. Chief engineer Washington Roebling was carried unconscious out of a caisson in 1872 and stayed seriously ill. His wife Emily passed his instructions on to the site.",
